# .loom/resync-ignore — paths Loom must not overwrite or delete on resync.
#
# See .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md for the full rule. Each entry below
# pins a deliberate, repo-specific divergence from the upstream rjwalters/loom
# defaults/ tree — a fix landed directly in this repo's installed copy
# because it was not (yet) upstreamed.

# #5552: restores the isDraft/exit-13 draft-PR exclusion from PR #5543
# (commit 0560777c), which a routine "chore: resync installed Loom surfaces"
# pass (4b4523e4) silently reverted ~2.5 hours after it merged, because the
# fix was a direct edit to the vendored copy rather than an upstream change.
# Pin these four paths so a future resync is blocked-and-explicit (or
# skipped once pinned) instead of silently reverting the fix a second time.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
#
# NOTE: entries use the ".loom/"-relative report form (per the convention
# documented in resync-installed.sh's header comment), NOT the repo-relative
# spelling, for the .claude/commands/loom/ entry below — is_ignored()'s
# fallback normalization only strips a leading "./" and ".loom/", so
# ".claude/commands/loom/judge.md" would NOT match the "commands/loom/judge.md"
# rel it is compared against; only the unprefixed form does.
scripts/judge-fallback-guard.sh
scripts/tests/test-judge-fallback-cap.sh
commands/loom/judge.md
roles/judge.md

# #5690: a `Part of #N` trailer written inside an inline code span is
# deliberately NOT read as a declaration (#5234's code-span exclusion, which is
# correct and unchanged here), so merge-pr.sh's partial-increment
# `loom:building` -> `loom:issue` reset (#3667) silently no-ops — the incident
# on PR #5686 / issue #5240. Two local fixes, neither of which touches the
# loom-daemon parser: a non-blocking pre-merge warning in merge-pr.sh
# (_warn_backticked_partial_increment_trailers + its two text helpers, with
# regression cases in the partial-increment suite) and a plain-text-not-
# backticked caution next to the trailer example in builder-pr.md (both
# installed copies, which must stay byte-identical).
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
scripts/merge-pr.sh
scripts/tests/test-merge-pr-partial-increment.sh
commands/loom/builder-pr.md
roles/builder-pr.md

# #5791: `discover_epic_children` (champion-common.md) gained a title-prefix
# containment source -- issues titled "[Epic #N] Phase " count as strong
# evidence even with no phase marker, no native sub-issue link, no epic-body
# task-list entry, and no literal "Epic #N" body phrase. Recurred twice on
# this repo (#5774's and #5784's children) before the fix landed directly in
# the vendored copy. Pin both the fixed file and its new regression test so a
# routine resync cannot silently revert the fix or drop the orphaned test.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
commands/loom/champion-common.md
scripts/tests/test-champion-epic-children-title-prefix.sh

# #5837: the follow-on half of #5791. champion-epic.md's own PER-PHASE queries
# -- "Step 2.75: Pre-Creation Existence Check" and "Phase Progression" ->
# "Detecting Phase Completion" -- still read the phase marker alone, so epic
# #5784's Phase 4 (child #5798, title-prefix only) counted as OPEN=0 CLOSED=0
# and would have been narrated "0 closed / 0 total". Both sites now union a
# phase-scoped `title_prefix_phase_issues()` with the marker source, and the
# zero-children case says "count unavailable" instead of asserting a zero
# (epic #3438's Phase 2 is prose-tracked only and is undetectable by design).
# Pin the fixed file and its new regression test so a routine resync cannot
# silently revert the fix or drop the orphaned test.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
commands/loom/champion-epic.md
scripts/tests/test-champion-epic-phase-progress-title-prefix.sh

# #5741: `_check_required_check_freshness`'s `loom-daemon merge-pr stale-checks`
# call is now wrapped in `forge_cmd_perm_safe` (the #6074/#6752 credential
# ladder), because the App installation cannot read branch-protection rules on
# this repo — `403 Resource not accessible by integration` blocked EVERY merge
# until an operator applied rung 3 by hand. That call lives in merge-pr.sh,
# already pinned above; these two suites source the extracted function and must
# therefore source lib/forge-helpers.sh, or every case fails with exit 127.
# They are pinned so a resync cannot revert the suites while leaving the pinned
# merge-pr.sh calling a function the harness no longer defines.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
scripts/tests/test-merge-pr-stale-required-checks.sh
scripts/tests/test-merge-pr-stale-check-redate.sh

# #5783: sweep-lease-publish.sh now blocks on a fresh lease from ANY other
# (host, sweep) pair on the same issue, not only a different host's; and
# worktree.sh's "existing worktree has uncommitted changes -> preserve" fast
# path calls lib/worktree-foreign-lease-guard.sh first (refuses on 2+ fresh
# leases). Landed directly in the vendored copies (5e193191) after #5781 was
# claimed by 4 same-host sweeps that collided in one worktree. Unpinned, the
# local-fix guard blocked every scheduled resync of this repo (exit 2 on all
# three dispatch hosts, 15-44 consecutive failures, installed Loom stuck at
# 0.19.487), so none of the other ~70 upstream updates arrived either.
# The two helper/test files have no upstream counterpart; pinned so a resync
# can never orphan or remove them.
# worktree.sh is the costly pin: upstream is actively porting it to
# loom-daemon subcommands, so unpin as soon as the equivalent fix lands in
# rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
scripts/sweep-lease-publish.sh
scripts/tests/test-sweep-lease-publish.sh
scripts/worktree.sh
scripts/lib/worktree-foreign-lease-guard.sh
scripts/tests/test-worktree-foreign-lease-guard.sh

# #5967 (and #4558): the post-worktree hook is REPO-OWNED -- Loom never ships
# hooks/post-worktree.sh; it is the documented per-project extension point
# (`uv sync --frozen --extra dev`, now bounded by a timeout). Pinned as the
# explicit declaration .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md recommends, so neither a
# resync, an explicit --clean, nor the installed-file write guard treats it as
# a vendored Loom copy. Its regression test is repo-owned too. Permanent pin.
hooks/post-worktree.sh
hooks/tests/test-post-worktree.sh
